# gitleaks false positives, suppressed by fingerprint (commit:file:rule:line).
#
# The marketing "surfaces" tabs render a SAMPLE captured event, and a real captured event carries a
# `dedupKey` — a provider-supplied idempotency key. gitleaks' generic-api-key rule fires on ANY value
# bound to a name containing "key", so it flags the demo values on entropy alone. They are made-up
# illustrative values in public marketing copy, not credentials, and the field cannot be renamed —
# `dedupKey` is the real API field name the tab is showing.
#
# The CURRENT file suppresses these inline (`// gitleaks:allow`). These fingerprints cover the same
# values in git HISTORY, which gitleaks also scans and which cannot be fixed at the source.
#
# ⚠️ Fingerprints are COMMIT-BOUND: a rebase rewrites the SHA and they stop matching. If the secret
# scan starts failing on these lines again after a rebase, re-derive them from the run log rather
# than adding a broader rule.
